para(report,f'Data source: {source}. The original dataset contains {len(df)} rows and 20 input features; train/test split is {len(Xtr)}/{len(Xte)}, stratified by binary label with random_state={SEED}. Class 1 (good credit) is encoded approval=1, class 2 (bad credit) is encoded approval=0.')
para(report,f'Missing values: {int(missing.sum())} observed. Numeric fields are median-imputed and standardized using training values; categoricals are mode-imputed and one-hot encoded with a reference class omitted and unknown categories ignored. Preprocessing is fitted only on training data. The seven numeric fields are { ", ".join(numeric) }. IQR-flagged training outliers: '+', '.join(f'{k}={v}' for k,v in iqr_outliers.items())+'. Outliers are retained: automatic removal could erase important credit-risk edge cases.')
para(report,'Logistic predictions use scikit-learn L2-regularized logistic regression; regression coefficient analysis uses statsmodels unpenalized binomial GLM on the same training-only transformed matrix for Wald intervals. Due to observational data and correlated predictors, coefficients describe association rather than causal impacts. Sex group is inferred from the dataset-coded personal status/sex field, which has important ethical and measurement limitations.')
report.add_heading('Part 1 — Model comparison',1)
